    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1365">

                <pb facs="1107" n="1097" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1097"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.76/6–249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-21T17:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>865. ConGen Tientsin tel 321, May 16, rptd Nanking 202, Shanghai 224, Peiping
                    140, Hong Kong unnumbered; Embtel 1172 June 2 rptd Peiping 189, Hong Kong 30,
                    Tientsin 36.</p>
                <p>Dept not in position object unilateral action Brit firm in establishing
                    Tientsin–Hong Kong radio communications since Dept has indicated to RCA<anchor
                        n="95" xml:id="d1365-f1"/> no objection its negotiating with Commie
                    authorities for North China circuit via Manila. No evidence at present Chi
                    Commie discrimination against RCA.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1365-f1" n="95" xml:id="d1365-f1-content">
                <p>Radio Corporation of America.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
